        "original_id": "3e485f27-5cd3-55df-8f79-97c06ba1d28f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Duluth Ship Canal, Florida\n- Projects: Cross Florida Barge Canal, Marjorie Harris Carr Cross Florida Greenway\n- People: Marjorie Harris Carr\n- Topics: federal supervision, environmental opposition, project cancellation\n\nFacts:\n- The Duluth Ship Canal was begun privately in 1871.\n- The Duluth Ship Canal was placed under federal supervision and maintenance several years after 1871.\n- The Cross Florida Barge Canal was a project intended to connect the Gulf of Mexico and the Atlantic Ocean across Florida for barge traffic.\n- Marjorie Harris Carr led opposition to the Cross Florida Barge Canal.\n- Two sections of the Cross Florida Barge Canal were built before the project was cancelled mainly for environmental reasons.\n- The Cross Florida Barge Canal is now officially the Marjorie Harris Carr Cross Florida Greenway.\n- The Marjorie Harris Carr Cross Florida Greenway is a protected green belt corridor that is one mile wide in most places.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "50b3ae51-82dd-5afe-869e-128abc061789",
        "text": "Page: Duluth Ship Canal. Sentence: Begun privately in 1871, it was put under federal supervision and maintenance several years later.\nPage: Cross Florida Barge Canal. Sentence: The Cross Florida Barge Canal, now officially the Marjorie Harris Carr Cross Florida Greenway is a protected green belt corridor, one mile (1.6 km) wide in most places.\nPage: Cross Florida Barge Canal. Sentence: It is named for the leader of opposition to the Cross Florida Barge Canal, a canal project to connect the Gulf of Mexico and the Atlantic Ocean across Florida for barge traffic.\nPage: Cross Florida Barge Canal. Sentence: Two sections were built but the project was cancelled, mainly for environmental reasons.",
